  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, you likely need a new roof if your roof is approaching 20+ years old, has widespread shingle or storm damage, shows signs of sagging or interior water leaks, or faces costly repairs that approach half the price of a replacement.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "if your roof is approaching 20+ years old, has widespread shingle or storm damage, shows signs of sagging or interior water leaks, or faces costly repairs that approach half the price of a replacement"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Exterior & Weather-Related Signs"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Aging shingles (15\u201320+ years): Asphalt shingles become brittle, dry out, and lose protective granules over time. Utah\u2019s high UV exposure, freeze-thaw cycles, heavy snow loads, and canyon/valley winds speed up wear.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              1,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Curling, cracking, or missing shingles: Shingles that curl upward or downward, crack, or blow off expose underlying layers to moisture.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              3,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Granules in gutters or downspouts: Heavy granule buildup in your gutters or on the ground below downspouts indicates shingles are shedding their protective coating.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Hail or high-wind damage: Bruised or missing shingles after severe Utah storms can compromise waterproofing even if leaks aren't immediately obvious.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              2
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Damaged or rusted flashing: Lifted, cracked, or corroded metal around chimneys, vents, and skylights often leads to leaks.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              4
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Structural & Interior Warning Signs"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Sagging rooflines: Dipping, bowing, or uneven roof lines point to trapped moisture, saturated decking, or structural framing issues that need prompt attention.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Ceiling stains, dampness, or attic leaks: Brown water spots on ceilings or walls, damp insulation, musty odors, or daylight visible through the roof boards in the attic signal active moisture intrusion.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              3,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Rising heating or cooling bills: Failing roofing materials and compromised insulation can make it harder to keep indoor temperatures steady through Utah winters and summers.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              3
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Repair vs. Replacement"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "A localized patch or repair may be enough if damage is isolated on a relatively healthy, newer roof. A full replacement generally makes more sense when damage is widespread, leaks recur across multiple areas, or repair costs approach roughly 50% of a new roof.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          1,
          4,
          7
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you share your roof's approximate age, material (such as asphalt shingles or metal), and any issues you've noticed , I can help you weigh repair versus replacement."
      }
    ],
